===Noun===
{{en-noun|p}}

# {{senseid|en|mechanism-machinery-etc}} A [[mechanism]] or [[machinery]]; the means by which something happens.
#: {{hypo|en|millworks}}
#: {{ux|en|Aged and degraded oil and grease can really gum up the '''works'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Great Expectations|I|III|37|Something clicked in his throat, as if he had '''works''' in him like a clock, and was going to strike.}}
# {{senseid|en|the works, all available fixings}} {{lb|en|with "the"}} Everything or [[everything]] that is available or possible; especially, all available [[toppings]] on [[food]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:everything}}
#: {{ux|en|I'll have a Behemoth Burger with '''the works'''.}}
# {{lb|en|with "the"}} Drastic treatment; [[abuse]]; the [[axe]] {{gloss|dismissal}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1954|year_published=1957|author=w:Ian Fleming|title={{w|Live and Let Die (novel)|Live and Let Die}}|volume=|location=London|publisher=Pan Books|chapter=The Big Switchboard|page=36|passage="Why don't we pull him in on tax evasion or misuse of the mails or parkin' in front of a hydrant or sumpn? Take him down to the Tombs and give 'em '''the works'''? If the Feds won't do it, we'd be glad to oblige."}}
#* {{RQ:Hornby High Fidelity|page=161|passage=It's not, really, but I didn't want consolation. I wanted '''the works''', and I got it, too.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[heroin]] or other [[drug addict]]'s [[equipment]]: [[syringe]]s, [[needle]]s, etc.

